      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I don't agree with this. I tried to salvage the idea but even that didn't sound right. It just gives an unfair advantage over people with no colliders on their model. And people would often cheat the system to cover themselves with colliders. Not one person who decided to be cheeky while others play fair, most people would try to gain this sytem and be unkillable.\nThe only fair mechanic that could be made is if the map creator itself would add actual shields that people can pick up in their hands and those would stop bullets. And that can be already done without any new scripts or anything",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-03-24T14:55:46.001Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A cool idea me and my friends thought of was the ability for colliders to deflect damage in maps using a combat system rather than acting as extra hitboxes as they do now. I do not see this being a major problem as if someone covers their entire avatar in colliders, block that avatar. I just think the idea of being able to have areas that do not take damage could just be fun and make the combat maps more dynamic. For example, a police officer avatar wearing body armor that would actually work.",
